Response: documented from human-service POST /orgs/audiences, which owns it; the gateway forwards it unchanged.","params":[],"body":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"brandId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"provider":{"type":"string","enum":["apollo","apify","crm"],"description":"The provider this audience commits to. apollo/apify when persisting a candidate from /suggest; crm for a brand whose audience is its uploaded contact list (served by crm-service — no filters/apolloAudienceId, brand-scoped). Omit for a neutral audience."},"nlPrompt":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"filters":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"nullable":true}},"apolloAudienceId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"Pointer to the faithful Apollo audience owned by apollo-service, when persisting an apollo candidate. Omit for a neutral / apify audience."},"crmUploadId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","description":"Bind this audience to ONE imported CRM source (a crm-service upload id of the same brand). Every CRM serve made under this audience is then restricted to the people of that file, so several bound audiences can coexist for one brand and each is independently pausable + independently costed. Validated against the brand's uploads at creation (400 if it is not one of them). Omit to keep the whole-brand behaviour. Immutable afterwards."},"crmPeople":{"type":"object","properties":{"signedUp":{"type":"boolean","description":"true = only people who signed up to the brand's product (a signup on its auth provider); false = only people who did not."},"replied":{"type":"boolean","description":"false = only people who NEVER wrote to the brand on any conversation channel (email, WhatsApp, LinkedIn, an answer to our outreach); true = only people who did."},"reachableBy":{"type":"string","enum":["phone","email"],"description":"Only people holding a phone / an email. A phone channel (WhatsApp, SMS) wants 'phone': a person served without one is burned for nothing."},"segment":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"nullable":true},"description":"A part of the brand's own CRM, as crm-service's PeopleSegment states it (passed through verbatim, validated by crm-service): dealStages [{stage, pipeline?}], dealStatuses, tags, reached / notReached (funnel steps), includeClients, includeOptedOut. Lists OR, keys AND; clients and opted-out people are out unless stated. Names come from crm-service GET /orgs/contacts/segments.","example":{"dealStages":[{"pipeline":"Sales Pipeline","stage":"Form Filled - No Appointment"}]}}},"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Bind this CRM audience to the brand's merged PEOPLE matching a filter (e.g. {signedUp: true, replied: false} = product signups who never answered) instead of to an imported file, optionally scoped to a `segment` of the brand's own CRM (e.g. {segment: {dealStages: [{pipeline: 'Sales Pipeline', stage: 'Form Filled - No Appointment'}]}}). Requires provider 'crm'; exclusive with crmUploadId. A segment crm-service refuses is a 400 carrying its reason. Every serve passes the filter to crm-service (same brand-wide no-re-serve forever); each served person carries its phone when crm-service holds one. Validated against crm-service's serve-stats at creation (its counts become the audience's Size / Remaining). Immutable afterwards."},"offerId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","description":"The offer this audience belongs to — a brand-service offer id. Scopes the audience to one distinct thing the brand sells; name uniqueness becomes per (org, brand, offer), so two offers of the same brand may each own an audience with the same name. Stored as-is: human-service defines no offer semantics and does not resolve the id (same as brandId). Omit to keep the brand-wide behaviour. Immutable afterwards."},"apolloCount":{"type":"integer","nullable":true,"minimum":0,"description":"Optional count snapshot the caller already obtained from /orgs/people/search/dry-run (apollo). Stored as-is; refresh-count re-computes it server-side later. Accepts null (e.g. an apify-source candidate carries apolloCount: null)."},"apifyCount":{"type":"integer","nullable":true,"minimum":0,"description":"Optional apify count snapshot (see apolloCount). Accepts null (e.g. an apollo-source candidate carries apifyCount: null)."}},"required":["name","brandId"]},"answers":[{"status":"200","description":"Created audience","schema":{"truncated":true,"firstChars":"{"type":"object","properties":{"audience":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"orgId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"brandId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"name":{"type":"string"},"nlPrompt":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"description":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"One-sentence summary of who THIS audience targets, distinct from the shared batch nlPrompt. LLM-generated at /suggest time. null for rows predating this field."},"provider":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"enum":["apollo","apify","crm",null]},"apolloAudienceId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"Pointer to the faithful Apollo audience owned by apollo-service ('one filter vocabulary' Wave 2). Set for apollo audiences; null for apify (legacy) rows and pre-Wave-2 rows not yet backfilled. The faithful filters live in apollo-service; the `filters` field below is human-service's opaque cache of them."},"crmUploadId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"The ONE imported CRM source (crm-service upload id) this audience is bound to. When set, every CRM serve made under this audience is restricted to the people that came from that file, so several CRM audiences can coexist for one brand and each behaves as its own audience. null = unbound ⟹ the serve covers the brand's whole imported list (the pre-existing behaviour)."},"crmPeople":{"type":"object","nullable":true,"properties":{"signedUp":{"type":"boolean"},"replied":{"type":"boolean"},"reachableBy":{"type":"string","enum":["phone","email"]},"segment":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"nullable":true},"description":"A part of the brand's own CRM, as crm-service's PeopleSegment states it (passed through verbatim, validated by crm-service): dealStages [{stage, pipeline?}], dealStatuses, tags, reached / notReached (funnel steps), includeClients, includeOptedOut. Lists OR, keys AND; clients and opted-out people are out unless stated. Names come from crm-service GET /orgs/contacts/segments.","example":{"dealStages":[{"pipeline":"Sales Pipeline","stage":"Form Filled - No Appointment"}]}}},"description":"The PEOPLE-pool filter this CRM audience is bound to: every serve draws from the brand's merged people (everyone its connected tools know, one row per human) who match it, instead of from imported files. null = not people-bound (file-bound via crmUploadId, or the whole imported list)."},"crmPeopleByStage":{"type":"array","nullable":true,"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"pipeline":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"stage":{"type":"string"},"served":{"type":"integer"},"remainingSendable":{"type":"integer"},"totalSendable":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["pipeline","stage","served","remainingSendable","totalSendable"]},"description":"A people-bound CRM audience whose segment names dealStages: crm-service's counts per stated stage (same snapshot as Size / Remaining). Entries overlap when a person holds deals at two of them. null otherwise."},"offerId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"format":"uuid","description":"The offer (Org > Brand > Offer > Campaign) this audience belongs to — an id owned by brand-service. An audience is assembled for one distinct thing the brand sells, so it is scoped to that offer rather than to every offer of the brand. null = no offer stated ⟹ the audience is brand-wide, the pre-existing behaviour."},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["suggested","active","paused","archived","deprecated"],"description":"Always 'suggested' (inactive) for a freshly-suggested audience."},"source":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"profileAudienceId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"format":"uuid","description":"The client PROFILE (WHO, a cold audience the client keeps or pauses on the Targeting page) this source list was built for: a buying-signal list (hiring now, new in role, recently funded) or a competitor-post engagement list finds THAT profile's people, screened against the profile's text. Pausing or archiving the profile pauses its lists; resuming it resumes them (unless the source itself is off). null on a profile itself, on a whole-ICP list built before profiles had their own (retired once they do), and on every other audience. Show profiles = rows with null here and channels[0].list = apollo_search; sources = channels[0].list."},"canonicalAudienceId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"format":"uuid","description":"When this audience is a deprecated provider-variant (e.g. retired '<base> [Apify]' from the apify->apollo migration), the id of its active canonical replacement. Membership/stats reads resolve a deprecated match to this audience. null for non-deprecated / unlinked rows."},"filters":{"type":"object","nullable":true,"additionalProperties":{"nullable":true}},"avatarUrl":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"Audience avatar as a hosted HTTP(S) URL. null until generated."},"apolloCount":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"apifyCount":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"countedAt":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"degraded":{"type":"boolean","description":"The chooser's verdict on the audience it picked for this row: true when no attempt apollo-service explored really answered the request and the least-bad one was chosen anyway. INFORMATION for the customer and the dashboard — nothing here blocks, filters or warns on it, and an audience is always chosen. false for rows created before the flag existed and whenever the chooser judged the pick a genuine answer."},"createdByUserId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"format":"uuid"},"createdAt":{"type":"string"},"updatedAt":{"type":"string"},"targetText":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"THE text of this audience: who the customer wants for THIS audience, in plain language. It is the text to show as the audience AND the text the pre-pay screen (Jev) judges every lead of every list below against, before any paid reveal. Distinct from nlPrompt, which a split shares across all its sibling audiences. null ⟹ see t","note":"Narrow the request (a filter, a limit, one id) to read the rest."}}],"needsTheirYes":false}

